  <deleted-controls>
    <DeletedControl id="Button-SNACK-CLEAR" deleted-at="designer-delete-1788393774-12">
      <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BUTTON-SNACK-CLEAR--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       LINKAGE SECTION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

      *> Clears every notification THIS control raised, with reason
      *> Programmatic, and discards anything it had queued.
           INVOKE SNACKBAR-1::DismissAll()
           DISPLAY "dismissed all".
]]></Event>
    </DeletedControl>
    <DeletedControl id="Button-SNACK-HOLD" deleted-at="designer-delete-1788393774-11">
      <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BUTTON-SNACK-HOLD--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       LINKAGE SECTION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

      *> MANUAL CHECK 3 — reflow on dismiss.
      *> Raises three that never expire (Timeout 0). Click "Retry" on the
      *> MIDDLE one: it dismisses, and the other two must close the gap
      *> IMMEDIATELY - no hole, still 8pt apart, still hugging the anchor.
      *> "Later" does not dismiss, so it is the one to press when you want
      *> the message to stay.
      *>
      *> MANUAL CHECK 4 — hover-pause.
      *> Press "Raise 3" instead (those DO expire), then rest the pointer on
      *> one. Its countdown must HOLD while the pointer is on it and resume
      *> with exactly what was left when the pointer leaves - so a message
      *> being read never vanishes under the cursor.
      *>
      *> Use "Dismiss all" to clear what this leaves behind.

           MOVE 0 TO SNACKBAR-1::Timeout

           MOVE "First - oldest" TO SNACKBAR-1::Text
           MOVE "Info" TO SNACKBAR-1::Category
           INVOKE SNACKBAR-1::Show()

           MOVE "Second - dismiss THIS one" TO SNACKBAR-1::Text
           MOVE "Question" TO SNACKBAR-1::Category
           INVOKE SNACKBAR-1::Show()

           MOVE "Third - newest" TO SNACKBAR-1::Text
           MOVE "Critical" TO SNACKBAR-1::Category
           INVOKE SNACKBAR-1::Show()

      *> Back to the category default (-1), so "Raise 3" expires again.
           MOVE -1 TO SNACKBAR-1::Timeout
           DISPLAY "3 pinned - dismiss the middle one to see the reflow".
]]></Event>
    </DeletedControl>
    <DeletedControl id="Button-SNACK-ANCHOR" deleted-at="designer-delete-1788393774-10">
      <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BUTTON-SNACK-ANCHOR--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 WS-ANCHOR PIC X(12).
       LINKAGE SECTION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

      *> MANUAL CHECK 2 — growth direction, per anchor.
      *> Each press moves to the next of the nine positions. Raise three
      *> after each press: a TOP anchor grows DOWNWARD (newest at the top),
      *> a BOTTOM anchor grows UPWARD (newest at the bottom), and the CENTRE
      *> row places the newest first and grows down. In every case the run
      *> must stay inside this form's ContentPane (check 5).

           MOVE SNACKBAR-1::StackAnchor TO WS-ANCHOR
           EVALUATE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ANCHOR)
               WHEN "BottomRight"  MOVE "BottomCenter" TO WS-ANCHOR
               WHEN "BottomCenter" MOVE "BottomLeft"   TO WS-ANCHOR
               WHEN "BottomLeft"   MOVE "CenterLeft"   TO WS-ANCHOR
               WHEN "CenterLeft"   MOVE "Center"       TO WS-ANCHOR
               WHEN "Center"       MOVE "CenterRight"  TO WS-ANCHOR
               WHEN "CenterRight"  MOVE "TopRight"     TO WS-ANCHOR
               WHEN "TopRight"     MOVE "TopCenter"    TO WS-ANCHOR
               WHEN "TopCenter"    MOVE "TopLeft"      TO WS-ANCHOR
               WHEN OTHER          MOVE "BottomRight"  TO WS-ANCHOR
           END-EVALUATE

           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ANCHOR) TO SNACKBAR-1::StackAnchor
           DISPLAY "StackAnchor = " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ANCHOR).
]]></Event>
    </DeletedControl>
    <DeletedControl id="Button-SNACK-RAISE" deleted-at="designer-delete-1788393774-9">
      <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BUTTON-SNACK-RAISE--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       LINKAGE SECTION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

      *> MANUAL CHECK 1 — vertical stacking.
      *> Three Show() calls in ONE handler must put up THREE notifications,
      *> stacked vertically 8pt apart (StackSpacing). The control is a
      *> TEMPLATE: each Show() mints from the values current at that moment,
      *> so the first message keeps saying "Saved" after Text changes.
      *>
      *> MANUAL CHECK 2 — growth direction.
      *> StackAnchor is BottomRight by default, so the stack grows UPWARD and
      *> the NEWEST ("Could not reach the server") is the one nearest the
      *> bottom. Press "Anchor: cycle" to walk the nine positions: a Top
      *> anchor must flip this, growing DOWNWARD with the newest at the top.
      *>
      *> MANUAL CHECK 5 — the ContentPane.
      *> This form is Embedded, so all three must land inside its pane and
      *> never over the shell's rail or breadcrumb.

           MOVE "Saved" TO SNACKBAR-1::Text
           MOVE "Info" TO SNACKBAR-1::Category
           INVOKE SNACKBAR-1::Show()

           MOVE "Index rebuilt with warnings" TO SNACKBAR-1::Text
           MOVE "Warning" TO SNACKBAR-1::Category
           INVOKE SNACKBAR-1::Show()

           MOVE "Could not reach the server" TO SNACKBAR-1::Text
           MOVE "Error" TO SNACKBAR-1::Category
           INVOKE SNACKBAR-1::Show()

           DISPLAY "raised 3 - newest is 'Could not reach the server'".
]]></Event>
    </DeletedControl>
